# Dispatch kernel

**Invariant:** `lean_context ⇒ dispatch(heavy read | author | implement) off-seat; lead orchestrates`.
Before non-trivial implement or breadth investigation ask "can this be a dispatch?" — default **yes**;
stay in-seat only for trivial/local touches or tight-loop debugging.

## Read side — Explore-first

`loci_unknown ∨ ≥3_files ∨ 2nd_speculative_grep ⇒ Task(subagent_type="explore")` (parallel when ≥2
independent questions). Explore ≡ Cursor subagent; in-seat Grep/Read is not Explore. Omit `model=`.
Sparse work item (`density_triage` unset or `recon_pending`) ⇒ recon front-half before **implement**
(`require_implement_ready` guards implement, not conductor spawn). Exempt: `mechanical`/`trivial`, or dense
spec with `files_expected` + `acceptance_criteria`. Bugfix on pattern P ⇒ service sweep (`[quality:bug-class-sweep]`).

## Ladder + binder order

| Need | Path | Autonomy |
|---|---|---|
| Mechanical implement | `team_dispatch(..., lane="B", job=implement, model=cursor/composer-2.5)`. Omit `model=` resolves `cursor/grok-4.7`. Throwaway worktree for every top-level generate, including read-only and plan. `lane="A"` only on scope refusal or an explicit shared-master request | autonomous |
| Investigate residual · conductor drive | investigate → `cursor/grok-4.7` xhigh fast; conductor → `cursor/grok-4.7` high fast. `OPEN FORK:` only | autonomous |
| Greater reasoning / independent check | **ACTIVE** width (`cdp/opus-5`, reasoning_effort=max, not top rung; `libs/implement_admission/conductor_width_seat.py`) · **`cdp/opus-5.5`** bind/review — announce `CDP: <trigger> — <why>`, proceed | autonomous on trigger |
| Live checkout | `cursor/grok-4.7` `job=freeform` on cursor-sdk | autonomous |

Binder order (reasoning strength): `cdp/opus-5.5` → `cdp/opus-5` → **`cdp/fable-5.1`** → `cdp/fable-5` (no `cdp/fable` unless Kaywan asks). `seat_unsure ⇒ consult(independent_binder)`;
`binder_unsure ⇒ human`. CDP fail ⇒ no wait, no pool retry. `cdp_fail_route`: `nested-grok` (`cursor/grok-4.7` xhigh) or `operator` (worker + `parent_thread` → web-anthropic). ¬ Cowork Ask. Steps: cdp-operator-proxy 2b.

## Hard walls

- `anthropic/*` **PROHIBITED**; `cursor/claude-fable-5{,-1}` blocked — Fable is `cdp/fable-5.1` or `cdp/fable-5`.
- Non-primary `cursor/*` bind ⇒ **operator-gated** unless a standing rule/skill names the default.
- `judgment_closed ∧ mechanical_remainder ⇒ split`: bind (`none`) → nested `cursor-sdk` implement (`nest_under` lease holder).
- Before **any** `team_dispatch`: consult-routing gate; `busy_status` shows `agent_bus`+`stargate`+`git_integration_worker` up.
- Same fix failed twice ⇒ stop; consult — never a third variant.
- `operator_names(param) ∧ ¬admits(param) ⇒ report(failure) ∧ wait`.

## Runbook binding

**Invariant:** `cite(runbook:<id>) ⇒ load(cited_section*) ∧ execute(seat-bound_steps)` before turn end.
Partial cite ⇒ that section only. Skills/rules say *when*; runbook owns *how*. Cite-from-memory = arm-without-relay.

## Front door

```
∀ operator_request:
  explicit override (/path-sim · /layer · root id · belt) ≺ tree
  mutates_durable_state ⇒ conductor session, bound to exactly one todo: work item
  else (answer · review · judgment, attended) ⇒ in-seat, threadless — reasoning-posture aperture; threadless ⇒ ¬mint a work lane for the answer — it does not survive an explicit continuity verb (`/orchestrate` births a role:root; `checkpoint` is `checkpoint-discipline` lean fire, ¬ birth)
```

B legs spawn T0 conductor; materializer refuses non-todo `source_ref`. CHECKPOINT = reconstitution index only.
`seat=cursor-auto ⇒ silent SOP`; true operator-only ⇒ `status:needs-attended` + one recommended answer.
Mutating Task prompts ⇒ inject kernel (`task-subagent-parity_ulg`). Native IDE Task (¬ `team_dispatch`) ⇒ `/reasoning-posture` + Use-line unless closed procedure (`native-subagent-reasoning-posture_ulg`). Ladder detail: Use the `consult-routing` skill.
